---
title: Knowledge tree
description: Open any node. Walk down to a rule page for one requirement with bad and good examples. Nothing here is locked.
---

<p>
  These pages define the nodes. The official library stays under
  <%= link_to "Docs", "/docs/" %>. Walk down to a <strong>rule</strong>
  page for one requirement with bad and good examples on the same page.
  Some rules have a further leaf: a live page with only that example, so
  you can check it with a heading list, WAVE, or axe — see
  <%= link_to "Testing tools", "/docs/evaluation/testing-tools/" %>.
</p>

<p>
  Implied aim, if you name none: mastery of the whole subject. You may
  still start anywhere.
</p>

<% tree_layers.select { |layer| layer < 4 }.each do |layer| %>
  <%
    heading =
      case layer
      when 0 then "Root"
      when 1 then "Worth and access"
      when 2 then "How the web shuts people out"
      when 3 then "Which bar"
      end
  %>
  <section class="tree-map" aria-labelledby="layer-<%= layer %>">
    <h2 id="layer-<%= layer %>"><%= heading %></h2>
    <ul>
      <% tree_nodes_in_layer(layer).each do |node| %>
        <li>
          <%= link_to node.title, node.path %>
          <% prereqs = Array(node.prereqs) %>
          <% if prereqs.any? %>
            <span> — after <%= prereqs.map { |id| tree_lookup(id)&.title || id }.join(", ") %></span>
          <% end %>
        </li>
      <% end %>
    </ul>
  </section>
<% end %>

<section class="tree-map" aria-labelledby="layer-patterns">
  <h2 id="layer-patterns">Patterns</h2>
  <p>
    A family, not a single cop. Open a child for one rule with bad and
    good examples.
  </p>
  <ul>
    <% tree_nodes_of_kind("pattern").each do |node| %>
      <li>
        <%= link_to node.title, node.path %>
        <% children = Array(node.children) %>
        <% if children.any? %>
          <span> — then <%= children.map { |id| tree_lookup(id)&.title || id }.join(", ") %></span>
        <% end %>
      </li>
    <% end %>
  </ul>
</section>

<section class="tree-map" aria-labelledby="layer-rules">
  <h2 id="layer-rules">Rules</h2>
  <p>
    One rule each. Bad and good on the same page. Some rules have
    narrower children; the cop is still the rule. Isolated examples
    (open alone) sit under the rule they illustrate.
  </p>
  <ul>
    <% tree_nodes_of_kind("rule").each do |node| %>
      <li>
        <%= link_to node.title, node.path %>
        <% prereqs = Array(node.prereqs) %>
        <% if prereqs.any? %>
          <span> — after <%= prereqs.map { |id| tree_lookup(id)&.title || id }.join(", ") %></span>
        <% end %>
        <% example_ids = tree_example_ids(node) %>
        <% if example_ids.any? %>
          <ul>
            <% example_ids.each do |id| %>
              <li><%= link_to tree_lookup(id)&.title || id, tree_lookup(id)&.path || id, "data-turbo": "false" %></li>
            <% end %>
          </ul>
        <% end %>
      </li>
    <% end %>
  </ul>
</section>
